      "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (triage judge, LongMemEval reader)",
      "anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6 (dream synthesis)",
      "openai:gpt-4o (LongMemEval judge)",
      "openai:text-embedding-3-large and -3-small (embeddings)",
      "voyage:rerank-2.5 (today's reranker)",
      "anthropic:claude-sonnet-5 (S8 labels)",
      "openai:gpt-5.6-luna (S7 synthetic transcripts)"
    ],
    "post_measurement_code_changes": "After the eval, feat/system-one-v1 gained the S1 budget fix (9f7794ec), key-aware defaults that turn on S7 and S9 when a TypeSafe key is present (3efee1e3; explicit settings win and eval runs never get key defaults, so the matched-pair arms are unchanged), and master merges through v0.60.25.0. The LongMemEval harness (src/eval/) and every reducer the analyzers apply are unchanged between fc9a1d45 and 9196543d; build and analyze reproduced the record at both commits."
  },
  "post_eval_fix": {
    "commit": "9f7794ec4a841f928e2c109d19b0d798ba4f91d4",
    "summary": "the per-query decide budget (decide.query_budget_ms, 1,500 ms) now starts at the first post-retrieval decide stage, so query expansion no longer uses it up; the S1 expansion arms (s_jev100x, m_jev100x) timed out on every question before the fix and were not re-measured"
  },
